TRADITION IS NOT TRUTH

Every generation inherits rules.

Habits become traditions.

Traditions become norms.

Norms become laws.

Over time, people forget why these rules existed.

A belief repeated for centuries
is not automatically true.

Reality does not change
because humans agree on a story.

Many things we call normal
are simply inherited assumptions.

Question what is real.

Think for yourself.

Truth does not need tradition.

Tradition does not create truth.
